a heap of 16 cells, each holding a header, a payload cell, or nothing

  a = alloc(4)   returns cell 1
      four cells and a header
      used 5 of 16 cells, largest free run 11

  b = alloc(4)   returns cell 6
      the next four cells and a header
      used 10 of 16 cells, largest free run 6

  c = alloc(4)   returns cell 11
      the heap is nearly full
      used 15 of 16 cells, largest free run 1

  free(b)        b was in the middle, so the hole it leaves is in the middle
      four cells came back
      used 10 of 16 cells, largest free run 5

  alloc(5)       needs six cells together, returns -1
      6 cells are free and the largest run among them is 5
      so the request fails with memory to spare

  alloc(3)       needs four cells together, returns cell 6
      the same hole, cut into a smaller piece
      used 14 of 16 cells, largest free run 1

  check: ok - every block is intact and no two overlap
